<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moscow Kremlin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> Kremlin is the fortified complex at the heart of Moscow, on a hill above the Moskva river. From the fourteenth century it was the seat of the grand princes of Moscow and later of the tsars, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> Italian architects rebuilt its brick walls, towers and cathedrals in the late fifteenth and early sixteenth centuries. It is the official residence of the President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow-kremlin.jpg" alt="Moscow Kremlin" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pavel Kazachkov from Moscow, Russia · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moscow_Kremlin_(8281675670).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
